Note digests:
{"note_id":50,"note_type":"Breast Imaging Report","summary":"Screening mammogram identified an asymmetry in the upper outer left breast; diagnostic mammogram and targeted ultrasound demonstrated a 2.3 cm irregular hypoechoic mass with angular margins and posterior shadowing, classified as BI‑RADS 5. An ultrasound‑guided core biopsy was recommended and completed on 2025‑02‑20.","flags":["screening mammogram","diagnostic imaging","BI-RADS 5","irregular mass","core biopsy","left breast","ultrasound"]}
{"note_id":51,"note_type":"Pathology Report","summary":"A core biopsy of a left breast mass revealed invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features and associated intermediate‑grade ductal carcinoma in situ; the tumor is estrogen and progesterone receptor positive and HER2 negative, with no lymphovascular invasion identified. The invasive component measures at least 1.1 cm across the sampled cores. Definitive tumor size and nodal status will be determined at excision.","flags":["invasive ductal carcinoma","core biopsy","estrogen receptor positive","progesterone receptor positive","HER2 negative","ductal carcinoma in situ","breast pathology"]}
{"note_id":52,"note_type":"Surgical Oncology Consultation","summary":"Patient presented for surgical oncology consultation after biopsy-confirmed left breast cancer; imaging showed a solitary lesion with no multifocal, contralateral, or chest wall involvement, and disease was staged cT2 cN0 cM0. The discussion covered breast-conserving surgery versus mastectomy, and the patient elected left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. No inflammatory changes or alternative pathology were noted.","flags":["breast cancer","surgical oncology","lumpectomy","sentinel lymph node biopsy","cT2 cN0 cM0","MRI"]}
{"note_id":53,"note_type":"Operative Pathology Report","summary":"The operative pathology report details a left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy, revealing a 2.4 cm invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, with intermediate‑grade DCIS and negative margins. All three sentinel nodes were negative, resulting in pathologic stage pT2 N0(sn). Post‑operative recovery was uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a resolving seroma.","flags":["lumpectomy","invasive ductal carcinoma","sentinel lymph node biopsy","negative margins","pT2 N0","postoperative seroma"]}
{"note_id":54,"note_type":"Medical Oncology Consultation","summary":"During the initial medical oncology visit, the patient’s resected left‑breast invasive cancer was discussed; it is hormone‑receptor‑positive, HER2‑negative, node‑negative, and >2 cm, prompting a genomic assay to assess need for adjuvant chemotherapy, and no staging scans were ordered given lack of systemic symptoms.","flags":["medical oncology consult","invasive breast cancer","hormone receptor positive","HER2 negative","node negative","genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy consideration","no staging scans"]}
{"note_id":55,"note_type":"Systemic Therapy Note","summary":"An intermediate-high genomic assay led to recommendation of adjuvant chemotherapy, and the first cycle of docetaxel/cyclophosphamide was administered with expected tolerance. A referral for adjuvant whole-breast radiation after chemotherapy and planned subsequent endocrine therapy were placed. The patient inquired about the impact of an in situ component, and it was clarified that the invasive component dictates prognosis and treatment.","flags":["genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy","docetaxel cyclophosphamide","radiation referral","endocrine therapy","invasive component"]}
{"note_id":56,"note_type":"Clinical History","summary":"The note records the patient’s past medical history of hypertension and hyperlipidemia, prior benign breast cyst aspiration, current lack of breast or systemic symptoms, ECOG performance status of 0, and adequate CBC/CMP labs for chemotherapy.","flags":["hypertension","hyperlipidemia","benign breast cyst","ECOG0","pre-chemotherapy labs"]}

