{"note_id":53,"date":"2025-03-18","note_type":"Operative Pathology Report","content":"Procedure performed 2025-03-18: left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. Final surgical pathology shows invasive ductal carcinoma, 2.4 cm, Nottingham grade 2, with associated intermediate-grade DCIS. Margins negative for invasive carcinoma and DCIS. Three sentinel lymph nodes examined, all negative for carcinoma (0/3). Pathologic stage pT2 pN0(sn). Post-op recovery uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a small resolving seroma.","summary":"The operative pathology report details a left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy, revealing a 2.4 cm invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, with intermediate‑grade DCIS and negative margins. All three sentinel nodes were negative, resulting in pathologic stage pT2 N0(sn). Post‑operative recovery was uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a resolving seroma.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"invasive ductal carcinoma"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"sentinel lymph node biopsy"},{"note_id":53,"text":"Three sentinel lymph nodes examined"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"invasive ductal carcinoma, 2.4 cm, Nottingham grade 2, with associated intermediate-grade DCIS"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["lumpectomy","invasive ductal carcinoma","sentinel lymph node biopsy","negative margins","pT2 N0","postoperative seroma"]}
{"note_id":54,"date":"2025-04-02","note_type":"Medical Oncology Consultation","content":"Initial med onc visit 2025-04-02. We reviewed that she has a resected left breast primary with hormone receptor positive, HER2-negative disease and node-negative status after sentinel node sampling. Because the tumor is over 2 cm and the patient is otherwise fit, genomic assay was sent to help estimate benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy. There is no suggestion in the record of a purely in situ process or benign lesion; treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer. Staging scans were not ordered because she has no bone pain, cough, weight loss, or abnormal liver tests, and presentation remains consistent with localized disease.","summary":"During the initial medical oncology visit, the patient’s resected left‑breast invasive cancer was discussed; it is hormone‑receptor‑positive, HER2‑negative, node‑negative, and >2 cm, prompting a genomic assay to assess need for adjuvant chemotherapy, and no staging scans were ordered given lack of systemic symptoms.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"resected left breast primary"},{"note_id":54,"text":"sentinel node sampling"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"genomic assay was sent to help estimate benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy"}]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"node-negative status after sentinel node sampling"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"resected left breast primary"}],"