{"note_id":51,"date":"2025-02-24","note_type":"Pathology Report","content":"Specimen: Left breast, 2 o'clock mass, core biopsy.\nFinal Diagnosis: Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features. The invasive carcinoma involves multiple cores and measures at least 1.1 cm in the submitted tissue. Associated ductal carcinoma in situ is present, intermediate nuclear grade. Lymphovascular invasion is not identified in this biopsy material. Estrogen receptor positive, progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative by immunohistochemistry. Comment: Overall findings are most in keeping with a primary breast invasive ductal carcinoma. This biopsy establishes malignancy; definitive size and nodal status are deferred to excision.","summary":"A core biopsy of a left breast mass revealed invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features and associated intermediate‑grade ductal carcinoma in situ; the tumor is estrogen and progesterone receptor positive and HER2 negative, with no lymphovascular invasion identified. The invasive component measures at least 1.1 cm across the sampled cores. Definitive tumor size and nodal status will be determined at excision.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":51,"text":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features"},{"note_id":51,"text":"This biopsy establishes malignancy"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":51,"text":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["invasive ductal carcinoma","core biopsy","estroge