{"note_id":51,"date":"2025-02-24","note_type":"Pathology Report","content":"Specimen: Left breast, 2 o'clock mass, core biopsy.\nFinal Diagnosis: Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features. The invasive carcinoma involves multiple cores and measures at least 1.1 cm in the submitted tissue. Associated ductal carcinoma in situ is present, intermediate nuclear grade. Lymphovascular invasion is not identified in this biopsy material. Estrogen receptor positive, progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative by immunohistochemistry. Comment: Overall findings are most in keeping with a primary breast invasive ductal carcinoma. This biopsy establishes malignancy; definitive size and nodal status are deferred to excision.","summary":"A core biopsy of a left breast mass revealed invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features and associated intermediate‑grade ductal carcinoma in situ; the tumor is estrogen and progesterone receptor positive and HER2 negative, with no lymphovascular invasion identified. The invasive component measures at least 1.1 cm across the sampled cores. Definitive tumor size and nodal status will be determined at excision.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":51,"text":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features"},{"note_id":51,"text":"This biopsy establishes malignancy"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":51,"text":"Invasive mammary carcinoma with ductal features"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["invasive ductal carcinoma","core biopsy","estrogen receptor positive","progesterone receptor positive","HER2 negative","ductal carcinoma in situ","breast pathology"]}
{"note_id":52,"date":"2025-03-03","note_type":"Surgical Oncology Consultation","content":"Seen 2025-03-03 after biopsy confirmation of left breast cancer. MRI from 2025-02-27 shows enhancement corresponding to the known lesion only, without multifocal or contralateral disease. No chest wall invasion. Clinical stage reviewed as cT2 cN0 cM0. We discussed breast-conserving surgery versus mastectomy. Given localized disease and patient preference, plan was for left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. Differential considerations from the original imaging report such as radial scar or complex sclerosing lesion are no longer relevant after tissue diagnosis. No evidence of inflammatory breast cancer on exam.","summary":"Patient presented for surgical oncology consultation after biopsy-confirmed left breast cancer; imaging showed a solitary lesion with no multifocal, contralateral, or chest wall involvement, and disease was staged cT2 cN0 cM0. The discussion covered breast-conserving surgery versus mastectomy, and the patient elected left lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. No inflammatory changes or alternative pathology were noted.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"biopsy confirmation of left breast cancer"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"plan was for left lumpectomy"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"sentinel lymph node biopsy"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":52,"text":"left breast cancer"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["breast cancer","surgical oncology","lumpectomy","sentinel lymph node biopsy","cT2 cN0 cM0","MRI"]}
{"note_id":53,"date":"2025-03-18","note_type":"Operative Pathology Report","content":"Procedure performed 2025-03-18: left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. Final surgical pathology shows invasive ductal carcinoma, 2.4 cm, Nottingham grade 2, with associated intermediate-grade DCIS. Margins negative for invasive carcinoma and DCIS. Three sentinel lymph nodes examined, all negative for carcinoma (0/3). Pathologic stage pT2 pN0(sn). Post-op recovery uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a small resolving seroma.","summary":"The operative pathology report details a left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy, revealing a 2.4 cm invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, with intermediate‑grade DCIS and negative margins. All three sentinel nodes were negative, resulting in pathologic stage pT2 N0(sn). Post‑operative recovery was uncomplicated aside from mild axillary soreness and a resolving seroma.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"invasive ductal carcinoma"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"left breast lumpectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"sentinel lymph node biopsy"},{"note_id":53,"text":"Three sentinel lymph nodes examined"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":53,"text":"invasive ductal carcinoma, 2.4 cm, Nottingham grade 2, with associated intermediate-grade DCIS"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["lumpectomy","invasive ductal carcinoma","sentinel lymph node biopsy","negative margins","pT2 N0","postoperative seroma"]}
{"note_id":54,"date":"2025-04-02","note_type":"Medical Oncology Consultation","content":"Initial med onc visit 2025-04-02. We reviewed that she has a resected left breast primary with hormone receptor positive, HER2-negative disease and node-negative status after sentinel node sampling. Because the tumor is over 2 cm and the patient is otherwise fit, genomic assay was sent to help estimate benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy. There is no suggestion in the record of a purely in situ process or benign lesion; treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer. Staging scans were not ordered because she has no bone pain, cough, weight loss, or abnormal liver tests, and presentation remains consistent with localized disease.","summary":"During the initial medical oncology visit, the patient’s resected left‑breast invasive cancer was discussed; it is hormone‑receptor‑positive, HER2‑negative, node‑negative, and >2 cm, prompting a genomic assay to assess need for adjuvant chemotherapy, and no staging scans were ordered given lack of systemic symptoms.","concepts":{"cancer":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"treatment recommendations are being made for an invasive breast cancer"}]},"metastasis":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"surgery":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"resected left breast primary"},{"note_id":54,"text":"sentinel node sampling"}]},"chemotherapy":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"genomic assay was sent to help estimate benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy"}]},"radiation":{"presence":false,"confidence":"high","evidence":[]},"lymph_nodes_removed":{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"node-negative status after sentinel node sampling"}]}},"cancer_status":["current"],"cancer_mentions":[{"presence":true,"confidence":"high","evidence":[{"note_id":54,"text":"resected left breast primary"}],"status":"current","affected_tissue":"left breast","metastasis":false}],"flags":["medical oncology consult","invasive breast cancer","hormone receptor positive","HER2 negative","node negative","genomic assay","adjuvant chemotherapy consideration","no staging scans"]}

